			"notes": {
				"rationale": "Duden lists low key, written apart, as an adjective (low key in jemanden verliebt sein), so it is German, not Foreign (de/foreign-unless-duden-or-german-grammar), and that headword is its Canonical Form (de/canonical-form-is-the-headword). The hyphenated low-key is the English spelling of the same word, not a mistake, so its Surface is a Variant of low key tagged Licensed, and its member is Standard, not Typo (de/variant-and-historical-status). This reverses 7eb1f043 (#729), which made low-key an ADJ Lemma of its own; ruled by the user on 2026-10-02. Duden gives no comparison forms, so it is not comparable and its Surface marks no Degree. low-key überraschend is Duden low key 2, colloquial 'unbedeutend', used adverbially as in low key in jemanden verliebt sein: only slightly."
			},
